---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro';
import { href } from '../lib/paths';
import { APP, APP_STORE, DOWNLOAD, PUBLISHER, REPO } from '../lib/site';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Download — HelloNotes for Mac, iPhone & iPad"
  description={`Get HelloNotes ${APP.version} free on the App Store for iPhone, iPad and Mac, or as a signed and notarised direct download for macOS. Requires ${APP.platforms}.`}
  heading={`Download ${APP.name}`}
  intro={`Version ${APP.version} — free on the App Store, or as a direct download for Mac.`}
  appSchema
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-[1120px] px-6 py-12">
    <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_320px]">
      {/* min-w-0: a grid item will not shrink below its content's min-content
          width, and a <pre> never wraps — without this the code blocks push the
          whole page wider than a phone. */}
      <div class="min-w-0">
        {/* Two channels, not one. The App Store is the only route to iPhone and
            iPad and the only one that updates itself, so it leads; the direct
            download stays because it predates the store listing, needs no Apple
            account, and is the build the checksum below describes. */}

        <!-- App Store -->
        <div class="rounded-card border border-line bg-card p-8">
          <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-5">
            <img
              src={href('assets/icon.png')}
              alt=""
              width="72"
              height="72"
              class="size-18 rounded-2xl"
            />
            <div class="min-w-[220px] flex-1">
              <h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.02em]">
                {APP.name} {APP.version}
              </h2>
              <p class="mt-1 text-muted">On the App Store · Free · Updates automatically</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-7 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
            <a
              href={APP_STORE.ios}
              class="brand-gradient inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-full px-6 py-4 text-base font-bold text-white shadow-cta transition hover:brightness-95"
            >
              iPhone &amp; iPad
            </a>
            <a
              href={APP_STORE.mac}
              class="inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-full border border-line bg-chip px-6 py-4 text-base font-bold text-ink transition hover:border-edge hover:text-emphasis"
            >
              Mac
            </a>
          </div>

          <p class="mt-4 text-center text-sm text-muted">
            Requires {APP.platforms}. Free on every device you own. The optional in-app
            purchases back the work and add an in-app support request; every feature of the app
            is included either way.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Direct download -->
        <div class="mt-5 rounded-card border border-line bg-card p-8">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.02em]">Direct download for Mac</h2>
          <p class="mt-1 text-muted">
            {DOWNLOAD.fileName} · {DOWNLOAD.size} · {APP.architectures}
          </p>

          <a
            href={DOWNLOAD.url}
            class="mt-6 inline-flex w-full items-center justify-center rounded-full border border-edge bg-chip px-6 py-4 text-lg font-bold text-ink transition hover:text-emphasis"
          >
            Download {DOWNLOAD.fileName}
          </a>

          <p class="mt-4 text-center text-sm text-muted">
            Requires {APP.minMacOS}. No Apple account needed. Also on the{' '}
            <a href={DOWNLOAD.releasesPage} class="text-link hover:text-emphasis">releases page</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <Prose>
          <h2 id="installing">Installing</h2>
          <p>
            From the App Store there is nothing to install by hand — open the listing for your
            device, install, and launch.
          </p>
          <p>From the disk image:</p>
          <ol>
            <li>Download <code>{DOWNLOAD.fileName}</code> and open it — a disk image window appears.</li>
            <li>Drag the <strong>{APP.name}</strong> icon onto the <strong>Applications</strong> folder shown beside it.</li>
            <li>Eject the disk image, then open {APP.name} from Applications or Launchpad.</li>
          </ol>

          <h2 id="first-launch">The first launch</h2>
          <p>
            Either way, {APP.name} opens with something in it. A collection called{' '}
            <strong>DefaultCollection</strong> ships inside the app — a short guided tour plus the
            user manual, written in {APP.name} and demonstrating the features it describes — and it
            is copied into your documents and opened for you the first time you launch. Nothing to
            choose, download or sign in to.
          </p>
          <p>
            When you want your own notes, use <strong>Open…</strong> and pick any folder of Markdown
            files — an existing vault, or an empty folder to start fresh. If you ever close the
            default collection you can bring it back from{' '}
            <strong>File ▸ Open Default Collection</strong>, or the <strong>+</strong> button at the
            top of the sidebar.
          </p>

          <p>
            Because the app is signed with a Developer ID and notarised by Apple, macOS opens it
            without a security warning. You do not need to change any Gatekeeper settings, and you
            should never need to right-click → Open.
          </p>

          <h2 id="verifying">Verifying the download</h2>
          <p>
            Every release is code-signed and notarised, so macOS checks it for you. If you would
            like to verify independently, compare the checksum:
          </p>
          <pre
            class="my-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-card border border-line bg-card p-4 text-[13px] text-body"><code>shasum -a 256 ~/Downloads/{DOWNLOAD.fileName}</code></pre>
          <p>It should print:</p>
          <pre
            class="my-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-card border border-line bg-card p-4 text-[13px] break-all text-body"><code>{DOWNLOAD.sha256}</code></pre>
          <p>You can also confirm the signature and notarisation with:</p>
          <pre
            class="my-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-card border border-line bg-card p-4 text-[13px] text-body"><code>spctl --assess -t open --context context:primary-signature -v ~/Downloads/{DOWNLOAD.fileName}</code></pre>
          <p>
            which should report <code>accepted</code> and{' '}
            <code>source=Notarized Developer ID</code>.
          </p>

          <h2 id="updating">Updating and uninstalling</h2>
          <p>
            To update, download the latest disk image and replace the app in Applications. Your
            notes are untouched — they are your own files, in your own folder, and {APP.name} never
            moves them.
          </p>
          <p>
            To uninstall, drag {APP.name} from Applications to the Trash. Your notes stay exactly
            where they are. Preferences live in{' '}
            <code>~/Library/Containers/com.hellotham.HelloNotes</code> if you want to remove those
            too.
          </p>

          <h2 id="source">Building from source</h2>
          <p>
            {APP.name} is open source. You can read the code, build it yourself, or open an issue
            on <a href={REPO}>GitHub</a>.
          </p>
        </Prose>
      </div>

      <!-- Sidebar -->
      <aside aria-label="Requirements" class="lg:sticky lg:top-[86px] lg:self-start">
        <div class="rounded-card border border-line bg-card p-6">
          <h2 class="text-sm font-bold tracking-wider text-muted uppercase">Requirements</h2>
          <dl class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-[15px]">
            <div>
              <dt class="text-muted">Mac</dt>
              <dd class="font-semibold">{APP.minMacOS}</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class="text-muted">iPhone &amp; iPad</dt>
              <dd class="font-semibold">{APP.minIOS}</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class="text-muted">Mac architecture</dt>
              <dd class="font-semibold">{APP.architectures}</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class="text-muted">Price</dt>
              <dd class="font-semibold">Free · optional support purchases</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class="text-muted">Account required</dt>
              <dd class="font-semibold">None</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class="text-muted">Internet required</dt>
              <dd class="font-semibold">No</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-5 rounded-card border border-line bg-card p-6">
          <h2 class="text-sm font-bold tracking-wider text-muted uppercase">Security</h2>
          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-[15px] text-muted">
            <li>✅ Signed with a Developer ID</li>
            <li>✅ Notarised by Apple</li>
            <li>✅ Runs in the App Sandbox</li>
            <li>✅ Hardened runtime enabled</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-muted">
            Published by{' '}
            <a href={PUBLISHER.site} class="font-semibold text-link hover:text-emphasis">
              {PUBLISHER.legalName}
            </a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-5 rounded-card border border-line bg-card p-6">
          <h2 class="text-sm font-bold tracking-wider text-muted uppercase">New here?</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-[15px] text-muted">
            The manual walks through your first collection, the editor and everything after it.
          </p>
          <a
            href={href('/manual/getting-started')}
            class="mt-4 inline-block font-semibold text-link hover:text-emphasis"
          >
            Getting started →
          </a>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
